  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Novolacs&nbsp;are phenol-formaldehyde resins with a formaldehyde to phenol molar ratio of less than one.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/bce89a9b-2b73-4072-b431-73850e2406b7-image.png\" style=\"width: 487px; height: 280px;\" /></p><p>The rubber obtained is also&nbsp;called Styrene butadiene rubber (SBR). In Buna-S, Bu stands for butadiene and, Na for sodium and S for styrene. It is vulcanised with sulfur. The rubber is slightly inferior to natural rubber in its physical properties.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8e53b179-9e27-4ca1-a4f4-c730da7907a9-image.png\" style=\"width: 379px; height: 140px;\" /></p><p>Glyptal- a polyester is formed by ethylene glycol and phthalic acid by step-growth polymerization.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d5455332-73a6-45f9-9fd8-23abe21036aa-image.png\" style=\"width: 527px; height: 140px;\" /></p><p>Dacron obtained by condensation polymerisation of ethylene glycol and terephthalic acid at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>420</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>460</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;using zinc acetate and antimony oxide as catalyst.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4e850628-0f8e-44f3-a570-476eab17f3ea-image.png\" style=\"width: 566px; height: 140px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
